/*
 * Declares the BitwiseIntOperatorValue class.
 *
 * BitwiseIntOperatorValue represents binary bitwise operations applied to two
 * integer operands. These operations manipulate the integer values at the bit
 * level and include operators such as:
 *
 *   - AND(`&`)
 *   - OR(`|`)
 *   - XOR(`^`)
 *   - left shift(`<<`)
 *   - right shift(`>>`)
 *
 * The result type is an integer, and the operator never produces an lvalue.
 * Throwers are inherited from both operands.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::binary::int_::bit
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/binary/int_/bit.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2024-12-04
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
